<Programs><Program Name="Demonstration"><Tags><Tag Name="NamespaceAlias" TagType="Alias" x:AliasFor="StartDelay"/><Tag Name="NamespaceDone" TagType="Alias" x:AliasFor="StartDelay.DN"/></Tags><Routines><Routine Name="Examples" Type="RLL"><RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N"><Comment>Invented start delay with a captured enable condition.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(Enable)TON(StartDelay,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N"><Comment>Observed done-bit use; equipment purpose remains a candidate.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(StartDelay.DN)OTE(MotorPermit);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N"><Comment>Separate reset occurrence for the same exact control.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(ResetRequest)RES(StartDelay);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N"><Comment>An alias and another timer writer remain distinct occurrences.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(Gate)TON(StartAlias,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N"><Comment>Sibling producer and reset conditions must remain separate.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[[XIC(Enable)RTO(RetainDelay,?,?),XIC(ResetRequest)RES(RetainDelay)];]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N"><Comment>Alarm wording is an authored hint only.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(RetainDelay.TT)OTE(AlarmLamp);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N"><Comment>Counter source condition is not an inferred count event.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(Enable)CTU(BatchCount,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="7" Type="N"><Comment>Count-down uses the same counter control.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(Gate)CTD(BatchCount,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="8" Type="N"><Comment>Counter reset association.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(ResetRequest)RES(BatchCount);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="9" Type="N"><Comment>Different counter members remain separate reads.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[[XIC(BatchCount.DN),XIC(BatchCount.OV)]OTE(Permit);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="10" Type="N"><Comment>Stored preset and source writes are separate evidence; repeated reads retained.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[MOV(AnalogValue,StartDelay.PRE)CPT(AnalogValue,StartDelay.ACC+StartDelay.ACC);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="11" Type="N"><Comment>Whole-object operation does not invent individual member effects.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[COP(StartDelay,RetainDelay,1);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="12" Type="N"><Comment>Incoming source condition is not a claim that timing occurs when true.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(Enable)TOF(StopDelay,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="13" Type="N"><Comment>Same-object TOF and reset observation; execution compatibility is not validated.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[RES(StopDelay);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="14" Type="N"><Comment>No matching producer is observed in this source fixture.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[RES(OrphanTimer);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="15" Type="N"><Comment>CONTROL is a documented reset target family, with effects outside this timer/counter interpretation.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[RES(ResetControl);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="16" Type="N"><Comment>Deliberately inconsistent mixed-family use for review; not executable code.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(MixedControl,?,?)CTU(MixedControl,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="17" Type="N"><Comment>Deliberate declaration and expected control-family mismatch.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(WrongType,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="18" Type="N"><Comment>Literal array-element association; bounds and runtime are not inferred.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(TimerArray[0],?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="19" Type="N"><Comment>A direct member of one exact array element.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(TimerArray[0].DN)OTE(Permit);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="20" Type="N"><Comment>Array-element reset exact match.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[RES(TimerArray[0]);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="21" Type="N"><Comment>Index spelling remains distinct from [0].</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(TimerArray[00],?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="22" Type="N"><Comment>Dynamic element remains explicitly unresolved.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(TimerArray[Index],?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="23" Type="N"><Comment>Nested control spelling and stored structure evidence.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(Equipment.Delay,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="24" Type="N"><Comment>Nested member association.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(Equipment.Delay.DN)OTE(Permit);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="25" Type="N"><Comment>Nested reset exact match.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[RES(Equipment.Delay);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="26" Type="N"><Comment>Two stored representations remain visible without choosing a preset.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(DuplicateTimer,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="27" Type="N"><Comment>Stored structure type disagrees with declaration; preserve the gap.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(ConflictingTimer,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="28" Type="N"><Comment>Absence of exported stored values does not mean zero.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(MissingDataTimer,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="29" Type="N"><Comment>Namespace-confounded stored field must not become accepted PRE evidence.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(ForeignDataTimer,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="30" Type="N"><Comment>Namespace-confounded alias keeps source navigation without accepted binding.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(NamespaceAlias,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="31" Type="N"><Comment>Rejected namespace use must not enter accepted readers.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(NamespaceDone)OTE(Permit);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="32" Type="N"><Comment>Missing declaration remains explicit.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(MissingTimer,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="33" Type="N"><Comment>Intentionally incomplete signature for diagnostics.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(StartDelay,?,);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="34" Type="N"><Comment>Intentionally empty reset operand for diagnostics.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[RES();]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="35" Type="N"><Comment>TIMER_T is distinct source data; no universal millisecond conversion.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(ModernTimer,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="36" Type="N"><Comment>Unknown members and deeper suffixes remain distinguishable.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[MOV(AnalogValue,StartDelay.Unknown)MOV(AnalogValue,StartDelay.ACC.Nested);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="37" Type="N"><Comment>Alias reads and repeated exact-member reads retain their occurrences.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[XIC(DoneAlias)XIC(StartDelay.DN)OTE(Permit);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="38" Type="N"><Comment>Sibling member read must not be attributed to the other timer condition.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[[XIC(StartDelay.DN)TON(RetainDelay,?,?),XIC(Gate)TON(StopDelay,?,?)];]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="39" Type="N"><Comment>Stored-state dependency in the incoming condition.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[ONS(Gate)TON(StartDelay,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="40" Type="N"><Comment>Opaque incoming behavior stays visible.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[INVENTED_BLOCK(Enable)TON(StartDelay,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
<Rung Number="41" Type="N"><Comment>&lt;script&gt;window.statefulFixtureLeak=true&lt;/script&gt; remains literal source text.</Comment><Text><![CDATA[TON(StartDelay,?,?);]]></Text></Rung>
